    "updated_at": "2020-01-23T18:22:36Z",
    "body": "I came across this issue after reading the [configuration doc](https://starship.rs/config/#terminology) and trying to customize `prefix` and `suffix` segments on some modules.\r\n\r\nSpecifically, this statement on the configuration page seems to be misleading or confusing:\r\n>Every module also has a prefix and suffix that are the default terminal color.\r\n\r\nWhich seems to imply that I can do something like this:\r\n```\r\n[kubernetes]\r\ndisabled = false\r\nprefix = \"[\"\r\nsuffix = \"]\"\r\n\r\n[aws]\r\ndisabled = false\r\nprefix = \"[\"\r\nsuffix = \"]\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nBut, it doesn't work on `starship 0.33.1`.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
