    "updated_at": "2020-09-19T09:07:35Z",
    "body": "Hey y'all any thoughts on potentially limiting the scope of the 0.45 release? Or possibly working to roll out some incremental 0.44.x releases to stomp out this feature & related issues?\r\n\r\nI recently converted to Starship from [Spacefish](https://github.com/matchai/spacefish) and so I definitely missed these base-level config options when I tried to mimic my fairly minimal prompt style from Spacefish by excluding things like via/on/etc. \r\n\r\nJudging by the relative inactivity here and in #1644 (and maybe other issues), it seems as if the work dealing with prefix/suffix for git/etc. could be made available before other new features are tacked on. I haven't dug through all the issues & convos but clearly lots of work has/is being done around these features.\r\n\r\nAgain, I'm not fully acquainted with the complexity of other moving parts surrounding this and I have no problem using a source build from master but thought I might provoke some discussion on releases/scope after I read @gerrywastaken's hopeful comment from a couple months ago 😛",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
